# Dormant safety net. Deploys now come from dist/ (wrangler.jsonc's
# assets.directory), and wrangler reads .assetsignore from inside the assets
# directory — so this file is only consulted if that is ever pointed back at
# the repo root. dist/ needs no equivalent: scripts/build.js decides what goes
# in it, so nothing dev-only is ever there to exclude.
#
# If you do repoint it: robots.txt and sitemap.xml must NOT be listed here —
# they only work if crawlers can fetch them. Same for _headers, which has to
# reach Cloudflare's asset storage for its per-path rules to apply at all
# (Cloudflare reads it as config, then 404s the path itself).
wrangler.jsonc
serve.py
package.json
package-lock.json
scripts
dist
node_modules
.claude
.wrangler
.git
.gitignore
.assetsignore
LICENSE
*.md
